[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3135874821","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3135874821","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3135874821,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc666acF","user":{"login":"paulloz","id":437025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzAyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/437025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz","html_url":"https://github.com/paulloz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T11:24:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T11:24:19Z","body":"Hello.\r\nI can't read the exception, but isn't the issue only with the hint name? Why do we need to also change the generated source content?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3135874821/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3143628479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3143628479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3143628479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67X_a_","user":{"login":"L2750558108","id":119792950,"node_id":"U_kgDOByPlNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119792950?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108","html_url":"https://github.com/L2750558108","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T07:58:30Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T08:02:12Z","body":"> Hello. I can't read the exception\r\n\r\nThese exceptions says the source generator generate code fail\r\n\r\n> but isn't the issue only with the hint name? Why do we need to also change the generated source content?\r\n\r\nBecause the solution includes adding \"@\" character before every class/struct name (not just before the name where the error occurs, as this introduces additional code for identifying keywords, and I have observed that the use of the \"@\" character in existing source code generators does not do the keywords check). Although this wont change any behavior, it causes the expected results of codes that contains class declarations change, and the existing source generator unit tests will fail. So I also changed the expected results of all failed tests","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3143628479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149713413","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3149713413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3149713413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67vNAF","user":{"login":"paulloz","id":437025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzAyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/437025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz","html_url":"https://github.com/paulloz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T08:58:16Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T08:58:16Z","body":"Yes, I understand once you've prefixed every type name with `@` the test results need to be updated. But my point is the issue as far as I understand is only with the hint name we provide to `GenerateSource()`. I don't believe the source content needs to be updated to fix the current issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149713413/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3150325186","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3150325186","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3150325186,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67xiXC","user":{"login":"L2750558108","id":119792950,"node_id":"U_kgDOByPlNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119792950?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108","html_url":"https://github.com/L2750558108","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T12:00:03Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T12:28:18Z","body":"The hint name is one part. If we pass hint name include \"@\" it would throw exception in AddSource function.\r\nAfter fix this with add a replace I find another part of the problem. If we use \"@base\" as class name or namespace name, the class name/namespace in generated code would directly become \"base\" (without \"@\" prefix) and lead to errors with different text (I didnt upload the picture of that case but I thought they are related so I fix them in the same PR).\r\nThe missing of \"@\" seems not cause by my change of adding replace which is only affect the hint name generating. It looks like the original class name/ namespace string the source generator gets dont have \"@\" prefix. Force add \"@\" prefix to class name/ namespace in generated code is to solve this","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3150325186/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151716296","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3151716296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3151716296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6721_I","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T17:21:58Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T17:21:58Z","body":"It shouldn't be required to escape the type names and namespaces manually, we're already using `SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat` which includes `SymbolDisplayMiscellaneousOptions.EscapeKeywordIdentifiers`. I tested the code you provided in the PR description and that seems to work with only the changes to the hint name.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151716296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151897293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3151897293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3151897293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc673iLN","user":{"login":"paulloz","id":437025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzAyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/437025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz","html_url":"https://github.com/paulloz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T18:22:07Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T18:48:53Z","body":"I can confirm I double-checked with only fixing the hint name, everything seem to run fine on my end.\r\n\r\nHere is the script I attached to a node:\r\n```cs\r\nusing Godot;\r\n\r\nnamespace @base\r\n{\r\n    public partial class Foo : Node\r\n    {\r\n        [Export]\r\n        public string Text;\r\n\r\n        public override void _Ready()\r\n        {\r\n            GD.Print(Text);\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nAnd here is the file emitted by one of the generators (the `ScriptPathAttribute` one, but they all behave similarly):\r\n```cs\r\nusing Godot;\r\nnamespace @base {\r\n\r\n[ScriptPathAttribute(\"res://Foo.cs\")]\r\npartial class Foo\r\n{\r\n}\r\n\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n~~Side note, I don't think your class name be prefixed with \"@\" if Godot's source generators need to run on it. It'd require the `.cs` file to also be prefixed, which (as far as my testing goes) seem to trigger a `CS2011` from CSC. Maybe that is what you intend to resolve with the rest of the patch?~~ Edit: No, after checking, that's not even a limitation on the classname/filename rule.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151897293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160833596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3160833596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3160833596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68Zn48","user":{"login":"L2750558108","id":119792950,"node_id":"U_kgDOByPlNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119792950?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108","html_url":"https://github.com/L2750558108","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L2750558108/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T16:32:03Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T16:39:47Z","body":"> Here is the script I attached to a node:\r\n> \r\n> ```cs\r\n> using Godot;\r\n> \r\n> namespace @base\r\n> {\r\n>     public partial class Foo : Node\r\n>     {\r\n>         [Export]\r\n>         public string Text;\r\n> \r\n>         public override void _Ready()\r\n>         {\r\n>             GD.Print(Text);\r\n>         }\r\n>     }\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nMaybe I didn't express myself correctly earlier, this part of the problem seems to be specific to the class name and not related to the namespace name.\r\nUse this script to test, with file name of base.cs\r\n```cs\r\nusing Godot;\r\nusing System;\r\n\r\npublic partial class @base : Node\r\n{\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tested again with only the change of 2 ExtensionMethod.cs file in the pr.\r\n<img width=\"466\" height=\"174\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9eefda1-0dda-4802-934c-29b3e7e65156\" />\r\nI could find these errors in compile.\r\n<img width=\"979\" height=\"449\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e953a70-443b-452a-9f9a-f42a2e2b72dd\" />\r\nThis is one of the generated code related to the test script. As I said, the class name dont have @ prefix automatically.\r\n<img width=\"530\" height=\"213\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f25b181-e98c-4ff5-9ee1-7b48899a2aa0\" />\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3160833596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3165736931","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106744#issuecomment-3165736931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106744","id":3165736931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68sU_j","user":{"login":"paulloz","id":437025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzAyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/437025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz","html_url":"https://github.com/paulloz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-07T21:19:42Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T21:21:06Z","body":"Ah! I see what's going on. Sorry for the misunderstanding, and thank you for clarifying.\r\n\r\nI didn't realize that we were still using an old extension method when writing class names (`NameWithTypeParameters()`). It uses `symbol.Name`, which IMHO isn't right. I'm pretty sure we can use `ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.MinimallyQualifiedFormat)` instead of it. That way, we wouldn't need to manually prefix everything with a `@` symbol.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>For context.</summary>\r\n<p>\r\n<img width=\"817\" height=\"201\" alt=\"rider64_pjJ5Oh4rQZ\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dfae7c25-af05-4612-bbca-ad2e43217d34\" />\r\n<img width=\"664\" height=\"96\" alt=\"rider64_kkZ